## Spatial and temporal transition map

| Window | Front | Living middle | Rear / residue | Required relationship |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0–5 min | Bergamot, lemon, aldehydic peel, wet Ginger EO | Linalyl body, citral flash, pale pepper | First violet-metal and Virginia cedar glints | Citrus exposes ginger without becoming the subject |
| 5–45 min | Ginger surface contracts | Jessemal, dihydrojasmone, ethyl linalool, terpinyl acetate, and clary reveal moist fiber | Leafovert, Dynascone, ionones, and basil expand behind it | Ginger changes physical state instead of vanishing |
| 45 min–3 h | Violet-green fiber and dry pepper | Ionone cloth, muguet air, and three cedar/vetiver grains | Tonka-sandal yielding chamber and mineral contour | Shared fibrous/woody/floral edges make one handoff |
| 3–8 h+ | Pencil-dry cedar-vetiver outline | Coumarinic and sandalwood interior | Koavone/Ambrofix/Norlimbanol pressure with Romandolide aura | The base recalls ginger through dry fiber, warmth, and cut |

All temporal language above is design intent, not observed evolution.

