| Violet Leaf Absolute 10% | Leafovert + Dynascone 10% + ionones + Scentenal 0.1% | Natural leafy-metallic complexity remains synthetic and simplified | **High-medium** | Purchase P1 only after the violet module survives |
| Haitian Vetiver EO | Indian Vetiver + Vetikon + Vetival | Current root is darker/earthier and less clean-dry | **Medium** | Purchase P2 after the wood recurrence is validated |
| White Pepper EO | Black Pepper EO 20 uL | The pepper is earthier and less pale/luminous | **Medium-low** | Purchase P3 |

Restored Lemon FCF and Virginia cedar remove two former approximation penalties. No missing item blocks focused computational evaluation; Ginger CO2, Parmavert, and Violet Leaf Absolute block claims of literal ginger/violet realism.

## Controlled blinded topology test — future work

Keep the 5,890 uL protected nucleus constant. Omitted modules are replaced one-for-one with DPG; all arms total 6,000 uL concentrate.

- **FIBER+ (80 uL):** Jessemal increment 50 + Clary Sage EO 10% 10 + Beta Ionone 1% 20. Tests warm rhizome body and aromatic recurrence into violet/vetiver.
- **RELIEF+ (30 uL):** Ebanol 10% 10 + Javanol 10% 10 + Scentenal 0.1% 10. Tests front/rear micro-contrast and carved finishing.

